255245379,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":true,"_score_margin_vs_hist":100.0,"_gate_piotroski":4,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":44.4,"_gate_spread":-0.05675989195218839,"_gp_spread":false,"_score_spread":0.0,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":0.0,"_gate_incr_roic":0.014104144158875858,"_gp_incr_roic":false,"_score_incr_roic":21.4,"_gate_margin_advantage":-0.05833410869088535,"_gp_margin_advantage":false,"_score_margin_advantage":13.9,"_gate_pool_share":null,"_gp_pool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":-0.012000337069183336,"_gp_margins":false,"_score_margins":38.0,"_gate_fund_growth":0.010471731326899837,"_gp_fund_growth":false,"_score_fund_growth":10.5,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.010877933315205396,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":23.2,"_gate_share_shrink":null,"_gp_share_shrink":null,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.01188490408673895,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":80.2,"_gate_insider_own":0.17416,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":100.0,"_gate_insider_buying":1.0,"_gp_insider_buying":true,"_score_insider_buying":100.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Utz Brands, Inc. manufactures branded salty snacks in the United States. The company provides a range of salty snack food products, such as potato chips, tortilla chips, pretzels, cheese snacks, pub and party mixes, pork skins, and ready-to-eat popcorn, as well as other snacks which include salsa and dips; and non-branded and non-salty snacks comprising partner brands, private label, and co-manufacturing products. It offers its products under the Utz, On The Border, Zapp's, Boulder Canyon, Golden Flake, Miguelito's, Hawaiian, Bachman, Tim's Cascade, Dirty Potato Chips, TGI Fridays, and Vitner's brand names. The company distributes its products through direct-to-warehouse, direct-store-delivery, third-party distributors, and direct-to-consumer. Utz Brands, Inc. was founded in 1921 and is headquartered in Hanover, Pennsylvania.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Howard A. Friedman | CEO, Principal Operating Officer & Director | Age 55 | Compensation: $1.7M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 3K people. Revenue per employee of $464K ranks in the below the sector median among Consumer Defensive peers, improving at 5%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $3K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $6K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 4\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (3/10).","financial_summary":["Utz Brands Inc is a mid-cap consumer defensive business with a $2.1B market cap on $1.4B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +1% over the past three years, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 1% against a 7% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, with gross margins sitting at 32%.","The business throws off $9M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 1 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 140.25\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 7.2\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 0.5\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 1.1%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 17% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.2\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.2) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Payout ratio of 2460% leaves essentially no coverage if earnings wobble","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom decile among Consumer Defensive peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"red","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Carries a 209% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":2.085137650631919},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 5.9% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 67/100): structural revenue/margin decline; leveraged balance sheet under pressure \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"GLP-1 and health-trend demand destruction \u2014 weight-loss drugs and wellness shifts are structurally reducing consumption in snack, beverage, and packaged food categories.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Large open-market insider purchases (net $1.0M) \u2014 management putting its own capital behind the business","Consumer Defensive sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 11% over 3 months","Consumer Defensive ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Consumer Defensive tends to hold up well as investors rotate into defensive names"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Utz Brands Reports Q3 2026 10-Q Filing: 88.6 Million Class A Shares Outstanding","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/news/a